### The API contract, one request at a time (VS Code REST Client: click "Send Request").
### Start the API first:  docker compose exec node node week12/api/server.js
### The login requests need a user. Add one first (the same email and password as below):
###   docker compose exec node node week12/api/add-user.js student@example.com "movies-2026" "Student"

@email = student@example.com
@password = movies-2026

### 1. The list: 200 and an array (at most 20, newest first). Public: no token, in class 2 too
GET http://localhost:3001/api/movies

### 2. Search by title: 200, only titles containing "star"
GET http://localhost:3001/api/movies?title=star

### ---- Class 1: log in ----

### 3. Log in: 200 { token, name }. Copy the token into jwt.io to read what's inside it
# @name login
POST http://localhost:3001/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 4. The wrong password: 401 { error: "Wrong email or password." }
POST http://localhost:3001/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "not-my-password" }

### 5. An email nobody has: 401, and the SAME message as request 4
POST http://localhost:3001/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 6. Nothing to check: 400 { error: "Email and password are required." }
POST http://localhost:3001/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### ---- Add and delete. Class 1: open to anyone. Class 2: the token is required ----

### 7. Add a movie WITHOUT a token. Class 1: 201. Class 2: 401 { error: "Log in first." }
POST http://localhost:3001/api/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "No Token Movie", "year": 2026, "genres": ["Comedy"] }

### 8. Add a movie WITH the token from request 3: 201 and the movie (request 9 deletes it)
# @name add
POST http://localhost:3001/api/movies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "title": "My Test Movie", "year": 2026, "genres": ["Comedy", "Drama"] }

### 9. Delete the movie request 8 added, with the token: 204, no body. Send it again: 404
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/movies/{{add.response.body._id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 10. Delete WITHOUT a token. Class 1: 404 (no such movie). Class 2: 401, before the route even looks
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/movies/000000000000000000000000

### 11. A token someone changed (one letter at the end): class 2: 401, the signature doesn't match
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/movies/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}x

### 12. "Bearer" missing from the header: class 2: 401 { error: "Log in first." }
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/movies/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: {{login.response.body.token}}

### ---- Still the same as week 11 ----

### 13. Break the rules (with a token in class 2): 400 and { errors: { title, year } }
POST http://localhost:3001/api/movies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

{ "title": "   ", "year": 1700 }

### 14. Not an ObjectId at all: 400 { error: "That is not a valid movie id." }
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/movies/banana
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
